  "question": {
    "text": "Using the expression&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math>, one calculates the values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> by measuring the corresponding angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#952;</mtext></math> in the range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;is exactly known and the error in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> is constant for all the values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>. As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#952;</mtext></math>&nbsp;increases from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math><span style=\"font-size: 10.8333px;\">,</span>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "t6STk",
      "text": "the absolute error in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> remains constant.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "QFUZY",
      "text": "the absolute error in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>increases.",
      "isCorrect": false,
